{'symbol': 'ABBV', 'date': '2022-02-24 08:00:00', 'title': "SECOND PHASE 3 INDUCTION STUDY CONFIRMS UPADACITINIB (RINVOQ®) IMPROVED CLINICAL AND ENDOSCOPIC OUTCOMES IN PATIENTS WITH CROHN'S DISEASE", 'text': 'NORTH CHICAGO, ILL., FEB. 24, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- ABBVIE (NYSE: ABBV) TODAY ANNOUNCED POSITIVE TOP-LINE RESULTS FROM U-EXCEL, A PHASE 3 INDUCTION STUDY, SHOWING UPADACITINIB (45 MG ONCE DAILY) ACHIEVED BOTH PRIMARY ENDPOINTS OF CLINICAL REMISSIONA,B\xa0AND ENDOSCOPIC RESPONSEC AT WEEK 12.1 U-EXCEL IS THE\xa0SECOND OF TWO\xa0PHASE 3 INDUCTION STUDIES TO EVALUATE THE SAFETY AND EFFICACY OF\xa0UPADACITINIB\xa0IN ADULTS WITH\xa0MODERATE TO SEVERE\xa0CROHN\'S DISEASE\xa0WHO HAD AN INADEQUATE RESPONSE OR WERE INTOLERANT TO CONVENTIONAL OR BIOLOGIC THERAPY.1 "THE RESULTS FROM\xa0THIS STUDY REAFFIRM\xa0THE DATA FROM U-EXCEED AND DEMONSTRATE THE POTENTIAL IMPACT THAT UPADACITINIB COULD HAVE ON CLINICAL AND ENDOSCOPIC OUTCOMES IN PATIENTS WITH MODERATE TO SEVERE CROHN\'S DISEASE," SAID MICHAEL SEVERINO, M.D.'}